INT. DRIVE-THROUGH WEDDING CHAPEL - NIGHT

A neon window. A speaker box. A cardboard heart.

REVEREND AMOS PLUMB, 60s, rhinestone collar, leans out the window, microphone on a stand. In the car below: BETTINA, 26, veil taped to her head, and DUANE, 28, tux jacket over a hoodie.

AMOS
Do you, Duane, take this woman?

DUANE
Yes.

AMOS
You didn't let me finish.

DUANE
Sorry. Yes.

Behind them, the car's back door opens. A third person climbs out. Wrong car. Wrong chapel. MARGO TALLEY, 40s, fast food uniform, a tray of milkshakes.

MARGO
Which one of you ordered the vanilla?

Everyone freezes. Bettina points at Duane. Duane points at Amos. Amos points at the menu.

BETTINA
We didn't order food.

MARGO
It says wedding combo.

AMOS
That's the second package.

Margo hands a shake through the window. Amos takes it. Duane grabs for it. They fight over the cup; it pops its lid and sprays all three.

Silence. Whipped cream drips from the veil.

Then headlights sweep the lot. Amos grabs the microphone, and his voice booms from the speaker box.

AMOS (O.S.)
Next couple, please pull forward.

Everyone scatters.
